xnu: the T8103 machine configuration may be built as DEVELOPMENT

The bring-up tree refused every kernel configuration but DEBUG for T8103 ("deliberately
DEBUG-only"). DEBUG is XNU compiled without optimisation and with every debug check; the
desktop now runs on it daily. config/MASTER.arm64.t8103 already defines DEVELOPMENT, and
nothing about the non-PPL, CTRR-not-engaged setup depends on DEBUG: -unsafe_kernel_text and
the serial console exist in DEVELOPMENT as well. RELEASE is still refused.

The same guard is in two assembly includes (osfmk/arm64/m1_cache_helpers.inc and
m1_progress_entry.inc: "#error ... require the explicit native DEBUG bringup configuration");
they accept DEVELOPMENT too.

Applied only for `--argstr kernelConfig development` (../kernel.nix); the DEBUG kernel's
derivation is unchanged.
UPSTREAM: for the bring-up tree's owner to decide.

--- a/src/Kernel/xnu/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/Kernel/xnu/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -147,10 +147,12 @@
         "Unsupported SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG='${SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG}'")
 endif()
 
-# The public non-PPL M1 development configuration is deliberately DEBUG-only.
+# The public non-PPL M1 configuration is for development kernels only: DEBUG, or DEVELOPMENT
+# (the same options with the DEBUG-only checks and -O0 gone; MASTER.arm64.t8103 defines
+# both). RELEASE stays refused: it has no serial console and no -unsafe_kernel_text.
 if(SILICONFOREST_ARM64_MACHINE_CONFIG STREQUAL "T8103" AND
-   NOT SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG STREQUAL "DEBUG")
-    message(FATAL_ERROR "T8103 bringup requires DEBUG")
+   NOT SILICONFOREST_XNU_KERNEL_CONFIG MATCHES "^(DEBUG|DEVELOPMENT)$")
+    message(FATAL_ERROR "T8103 bringup requires DEBUG or DEVELOPMENT")
 endif()
 
 file(MAKE_DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/xnu_header_install)
--- a/src/Kernel/xnu/osfmk/arm64/m1_cache_helpers.inc
+++ b/src/Kernel/xnu/osfmk/arm64/m1_cache_helpers.inc
@@ -7,8 +7,8 @@
  * No allocation, call, stack use, callee-saved GPR clobber or success stub.
  * Ranges must be valid kernel VAs with non-wrapping end addresses.
  */
-#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_T8103) || !DARWIN_LAB_M1_BRINGUP || !DEBUG
-#error "M1 cache wrappers require the explicit native DEBUG bringup configuration"
+#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_T8103) || !DARWIN_LAB_M1_BRINGUP || !(DEBUG || DEVELOPMENT)
+#error "M1 cache wrappers require the explicit native DEBUG or DEVELOPMENT bringup configuration"
 #endif
 
 	.text
--- a/src/Kernel/xnu/osfmk/arm64/m1_progress_entry.inc
+++ b/src/Kernel/xnu/osfmk/arm64/m1_progress_entry.inc
@@ -5,8 +5,8 @@
  * still continues through the original page-table/MMU/arm_init path.
  * The physical UART is valid only here, before the stage-1 MMU is enabled.
  */
-#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_T8103) || !DARWIN_LAB_M1_BRINGUP || !DEBUG
-#error "M1 progress requires the explicit native DEBUG bringup configuration"
+#if !defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_T8103) || !DARWIN_LAB_M1_BRINGUP || !(DEBUG || DEVELOPMENT)
+#error "M1 progress requires the explicit native DEBUG or DEVELOPMENT bringup configuration"
 #endif
 
 	movz x1, #0x3520, lsl #16
